{
 "_comment": "Post-S53 (Chris): Open lists contributed from play — each one a deck that did something in a Convocation, added to the Open's library beside the planner's twelve. pnpm open:gen validates (sixty, legal in the Open) and appends them; its strength is measured by pnpm open:rr before it can enter the field (OPEN_MEANS). Grows as Convocations are played. S55 (ADR-161): a list may declare archetype \"combo\" with a `plan` (setup / start / dig / fuel / answers — packages/agents/src/plans.ts has the shape) and its registered `sideboard`.",
 "archived": {
  "loop": "S56 (ADR-164): redundant with the Coin — 31 of its 37 nonland cards shared, matchup profiles r = 0.88, worse against eleven of the other twelve. Last measured 53 (pilot 106, sixteen lists).",
  "larder": "Post-S57 (Chris, 2026-10-07; ADR-165's exit): last in five measures (31 on the S57 table with its plan). Acceleration, a green mana base and a mono-green-with-Zombify build all measured flat or worse (handoff). The Pall does its job a turn faster. Its plan (goal: once) stays as the vocabulary's second customer.",
  "undertow": "Post-S58 (Chris, 2026-10-08): replaced by the Writ, his 5–0 Dimir Control list (53.6% in the AI's hands against the Undertow's 40). Last measured 40 (pilot 111, S58's table).",
  "cinder": "Post-S58 (Chris, 2026-10-08): replaced by the Rabble, the goblin build of mono-red (68.9% in the AI's hands in the Cinder's seat, where the Cinder stood at 44). Last measured 44 (pilot 113).",
  "ford": "Post-S59 (Chris and the planner, 2026-10-10): replaced by its overhaul, the Tollgate (46.9 against the Ford's 38.3 in game one, paired; 44 against 37.5 in matches). Last measured 38 in game one and 37.5 in matches (eighteen lists, pilot 120).",
  "reaper": "Post-S59 (Chris, 2026-10-10): superseded by Reaper Clio, the four-colour build of the same deck, which beat it nine matches in ten (74 against 56 in matches against the field). Last measured 54 in game one and 55.6 in matches (eighteen lists, pilot 120).",
  "locks": "S60 (ADR-174): a planner seed in the bottom three on three tables, with no revision from play — Esper control has no role the Writ and Countersnake do not fill. Last measured 36 in game one and 34.8 in matches (eighteen lists, pilot 121). Its fifteen and its guide are kept with it.",
  "tally": "S60 (ADR-174): a planner seed in the bottom three on three tables — two Izzet lists in the field, this one at 39 in matches. Last measured 43 in game one and 38.9 in matches (eighteen lists, pilot 121).",
  "enchantress": "S60 (ADR-174): the one overhaul attempt reached 38.5 in matches (33.4 as it stood: four Reaper's Forerunners for the Guides and two Mongooses, a Vitalist for the Glare, a fourth Destiny and a second Vitalist for the Keepers), under the 45 the ruling asked. Last measured 39 in game one and 36.1 in matches (eighteen lists, pilot 121).",
  "coin": "Post-S60 (Chris, 2026-10-11): replaced, with the Hearth, by Mardu Control — the same Usher, Blood Artist and Warden cards in a controlling build that measured 63 in matches against the field where the Coin stood at 60, and better than the Coin against eleven of thirteen shared opponents (the Pall and the Writ the exceptions). Two Usher decks stay: the Pall's combo and this. Last measured 51 in game one and 59.9 in matches (fifteen lists, pilot 122).",
  "hearth": "Post-S60 (Chris, 2026-10-11): replaced, with the Coin, by Mardu Control (63 in matches against the field where the Hearth stood at 60). The Hearth was the better of the two against the Pall (62 against Mardu Control's 43), Countersnake and the Writ; Mardu Control the better against the Rabble (48 against 23), Reaper Clio, the Sweep, the Kiln and the Coin. Last measured 53 in game one and 59.9 in matches (fifteen lists, pilot 122)."
 },
